            <ArticleTitle>[Structure of diseases and signs of connective tissue dysplasia in suspected ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>52-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Seventy-six males, complaining of atypical chest pain, were investigated. Mitral prolapse was the most common condition, detected in 45% of these patients, 40% of those displaying signs of connective-tissue dysplasia: increased skin elasticity and joint mobility, and subcutaneous nodules on the shins. The probability of mitral prolapse detection is high in the presence of signs of connective-tissue dysplasia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
